7. Graph Execution Engine

7.1 Graph Structure

```typescript
interface Graph {
  id: string;
  version: string;
  nodes: Node[];
  edges: Edge[];
  metadata: {
    author: string;
    created: timestamp;
    tags: string[];
  };
}

interface Node {
  id: string;
  type: 'birth' | 'think' | 'act' | 'condition' | 'loop' | 'parallel' | 'subgraph';
  config: Record<string, any>;
  repo_target?: string; // Which repo to delegate to
  timeout_ms: number;
  retry_policy: RetryPolicy;
}

interface Edge {
  from: string;
  to: string;
  condition?: string; // Conditional routing expression
  weight?: number; // For probabilistic routing
}
```

7.2 Execution Modes
- Synchronous — Block until complete, return full result
- Asynchronous — Submit job, return job_id, poll or webhook
- Streaming — Real-time output as nodes complete (WebSocket)
- Scheduled — Execute at specific time or on trigger

